        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: expose replayed chat.send errors to retrying clients",
        "body": "Closes #103703\n\nRelated: #98203\nSupersedes: #98206\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where backend clients retrying a failed `chat.send` with the same idempotency key could not tell that the Gateway had returned a stored result. A cached retryable error therefore looked fresh and could be resubmitted until the client's retry budget was exhausted.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis replaces the broad metadata forwarding proposed in #98206 with a narrow negotiated contract:\n\n- `response-replay` is an explicit client capability.\n- The only wire metadata is the closed JSON shape `{ replayed: true }`.\n- Core Gateway handlers use an internal responder with a dedicated wire-metadata argument.\n- Plugin handlers retain the existing four-argument responder contract; the plugin adapter strips any attempted fifth argument.\n- Clients without the capability receive the unchanged strict response envelope.\n- The official TypeScript Gateway client advertises the capability and exposes `GatewayClientRequestError.replayed`, providing an in-tree consumer.\n\n`runId`, diagnostic `error`/`channel` values, and plugin metadata are never copied into the response metadata object.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRetrying clients can stop resubmitting the same idempotency key after the Gateway returns a stored retryable error. Existing clients and native apps that do not advertise `response-replay` see no new response-frame fields.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Rebased onto `6f9a607b90393b14d769ec4696b99a6dc057498f`; current PR head is `4d4b07963d666bc2ac3ac5665b72998b3ab109da`.\n- Exact-head loopback WebSocket proof passed through the current `message-handler.ts` and official `GatewayClient`:\n  - legacy `caps: []` received the unchanged response with no `meta`;\n  - the official client advertised `response-replay`, received only `meta: { replayed: true }`, and raised `GatewayClientRequestError` with `gatewayCode: \"UNAVAILABLE\"`, `retryable: true`, and `replayed: true`;\n  - log-only sentinels were absent from both wire responses.\n- Plugin ownership regression passed: a plugin's attempted fifth responder argument is removed before the core responder is called.\n- Full plugin loader suite passed: 175/175.\n- Focused protocol, client, Gateway handler, and cached-chat suites passed: 247/247 across 9 test files.\n- Plugin SDK surface check passed with no forbidden package exports.\n- Full TypeScript project graph passed: `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -b tsconfig.projects.json`.\n- Protocol and Swift models remain aligned; `ResponseFrame.meta` is optional and legacy clients retain the strict old envelope.\n\nThe earlier live WebSocket capture in #98206 establishes the original dropped-metadata behavior. The current exact-head proof separately verifies the negotiated compatibility, core-only producer boundary, and official-client behavior introduced by this PR.\n",
        "branch": "fix/gate-deduplicated-chat-responses",
